DoD 2, red first. Edit only moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/toolwindow/BoardMovesTest.kt, with the Edit tool (TOOL-witness rail).

Append two JUnit 4 tests after everyPreviousMoveIsLegalForTheDaemon. The file already imports assertEquals, assertFalse, assertNull and assertTrue, so add no import:

```
@Test fun nextFollowsTheWorkflowOrder() {
    assertEquals("PLANNING", BoardMoves.next("BACKLOG"))
    assertEquals("AWAITING_APPROVAL", BoardMoves.next("PLANNING"))
    assertEquals("WORKING", BoardMoves.next("AWAITING_APPROVAL"))
    assertEquals("REVIEW", BoardMoves.next("WORKING"))
    assertEquals("DONE", BoardMoves.next("REVIEW"))
}

@Test fun doneBlockedArchivedAndUnknownHaveNoNext() {
    for (s in listOf("DONE", "BLOCKED", "ARCHIVED", "", "NOT_A_STATUS")) {
        assertNull("status '$s'", BoardMoves.next(s))
        assertFalse("status '$s'", BoardMoves.hasNext(s))
    }
    for (s in listOf("BACKLOG", "PLANNING", "AWAITING_APPROVAL", "WORKING", "REVIEW")) {
        assertTrue("status '$s'", BoardMoves.hasNext(s))
    }
}
```

The AWAITING_APPROVAL assertion matters: handleNext returns early on a null next, so a null there would silently remove the approve ▶. Leave the validTransitions copy at :10-21 untouched. The new cases do not read it, and the row scopes that fix to "only if the new cases depend on it".

